Q: How do I change an image on hover over in WPF? A: <p>You need to use a <code>Trigger</code> on the <code>IsMouseOver</code> property to modify the <code>Source</code> of the Image:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;Image&gt;
  &lt;Image.Style&gt;
    &lt;Style TargetType=&quot;{x:Type Image}&quot;&gt;
      &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Source&quot; Value=&quot;C:\Image1.jpg&quot;/&gt;
      &lt;Style.Triggers&gt;
        &lt;Trigger Property=&quot;IsMouseOver&quot; Value=&quot;True&quot;&gt;
          &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Source&quot; Value=&quot;C:\Image2.jpg&quot;/&gt;
        &lt;/Trigger&gt;
      &lt;/Style.Triggers&gt;
    &lt;/Style&gt;
  &lt;/Image.Style&gt;
&lt;/Image&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Note that <code>Triggers</code> can only be used inside <code>Styles</code>, and in order for a <code>Trigger</code> to change a property that property's value must be set by the <code>Style</code> and not set explicitly on the element.</p>
